\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Both formats have exact solutions, but step training learns while outcome training stays at chance.} (a)~Counting \texttt  a in \texttt  {banana}, modulo $3$. The same architecture holds an exact executor for each format. (b)~Zero-readout counting, $n=16$, $K=2$: median exact continuation accuracy over ten paired seeds; shading spans all seeds. At $8$k updates, eight step seeds reach $90\%$ exact accuracy; no outcome seed does. Dashed: exact executors; dotted: chance answer accuracy. (c)~A separate measurement with the standard nonzero readout at $n=8$, $K=2$, $\sigma =0.02$: normalized target and Jacobian energy barely overlap by degree. The Jacobian has $99.6\%$ of its energy at degree $0$; full spectra are in \cref  {fig:overlap}.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Both formats have exact solutions, but step training learns while outcome training stays at chance.} (a)~Counting \texttt a in \texttt {banana}, modulo $3$. The same architecture holds an exact executor for each format. (b)~Zero-readout counting, $n=16$, $K=2$: median exact continuation accuracy over ten paired seeds; shading spans all seeds. At $8$k updates, eight step seeds reach $90\%$ exact accuracy; no outcome seed does. Dashed: exact executors; dotted: chance answer accuracy. (c)~A separate measurement with the standard nonzero readout at $n=8$, $K=2$, $\initscale =0.02$: normalized target and Jacobian energy barely overlap by degree. The Jacobian has $99.6\%$ of its energy at degree $0$; full spectra are in \cref {fig:overlap}}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:overview@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][1][]2}{}{}{}}
