\newlabel{tab:matched}{{2}{7}{\textbf {Rule credit has polynomial horizon cost; outcome interaction credit has exponential cost.} Norm of each part of the gradient at initialization, with the scale of its theorem bound (constants omitted). Counting, $K=2$, $\mixrate =\frac 12$, $\initscale =0.02$, exact over all words (\cref {app:exp-regime})}{table.caption.12}{}}
