\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Modulo-$2$ outcome runs remain unsolved at the tested horizons.} Exact-continuation accuracy (\%) on held-out words; a run is solved if it reaches $\ge 90\%$. Paired formats share $\theta _0$, data and batches. Panel (b) excludes $n=4$, which has fewer distinct prompts than the training set. At $\sigma =0.5$ both losses are unstable at this learning rate; the $\sigma ^6$ credit scale at $\sigma =0.1$ is $5^6\approx 1.6\times 10^4$ times that at $0.02$, a qualitative comparison that the theorems do not certify. Both handcoded executors are exact at every horizon.}}{34}{table.caption.68}\protected@file@percent }
